      "language": "Solidity",
      "description": "An attacker drained Chainflip's Ethereum vault using a valid Schnorr signature associated with the protocol's aggregate validator signing key. The malicious transferBatch request used an anomalous nonce outside the normal signing sequence, indicating that the signature was generated outside Chainflip's usual authorization process. The attacker withdrew approximately $4.86M in ETH, USDC and USDT, converted the stablecoins to ETH, and deposited 2,909 ETH into Tornado Cash. A compromise of the validator signing system is suspected, but the exact root cause remains unconfirmed"
    },
